A||||30||Songman||Ck3 kits||||1||
Z||000000||Songman||05-24-2001||07:01 PM||||I just got an e-mail from Blaine Kennedy at Ck3 about their monthly specials. They have 3 512 Spyder kits that are really cool looking cars. The kit is on sale for $4495, down from  $6950.<P>Here's the link...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.ck3.com/protected/512ms/512ms.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ck3.com/protected/512ms/512ms.html</A> <P>Now I have a question. I remember the name Blaine Kennedy from another kit car company in the past. Anyone else remember this?<P>Ck3 is located in Calgary, Alberta Canada for any of you up there that are thinking about a kit.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrgone||05-24-2001||08:05 PM||||WOW||||reg||1
Z||000002||pherder||05-24-2001||09:24 PM||||You might want to read this ...<P> <A HREF="http://www.kitcar.com/consumeralert/home.html#anchor-Ck3" TARGET=_blank>http://www.kitcar.com/consumeralert/home.html#anchor-Ck3</A> <P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000003||rockcrawl||05-24-2001||09:49 PM||||I've never seen one in person, but CK3's cars look top notch. They go all the way to fool people. I've shared a few emails with Blaine. He seems like a nice enough guy. I've also heard that he is somewhat of a shadey character. I asked him about his lights for my 512TR, and he sent me some detailed pics and measurements of some lights that looked like they were copied from the Ferrari website. When I look at pics of their 512TRs, they all have shitty looking reproduction lights in them. I'm affraid I would have shelled out the $200 and got something other than what he showed me, so I never ordered them. Make sure you get all the details in writing. Heres something you'll want to read <A HREF="http://www.kitcar.com/consumeralert/home.html#anchor-Ck3" TARGET=_blank>http://www.kitcar.com/consumeralert/home.html#anchor-Ck3</A> <BR>Don't take that too seriously, it seems like Curt Scott has a problem with every kit car manufacturer.<BR>CK3 also has (or had) addresses in LasVegas, Seattle, and Vancouver. The brochures and photos I got came from Nevada. They do a hell of a job presenting their cars. I have never seen such high quality advertising from any other kit car maker. I'm not sure that's a good thing. <BR> Daleford (from this forum) is building a CK3 Koenig Rossa. I believe he got it from an ex-employee of CK3, not from Blaine.<P>Jon<P>p.s. tell Blaine you want a "spare" windshield with your kit, then give it to me!<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Archie||05-24-2001||11:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rockcrawl:<BR><B> <BR>Don't take that too seriously, it seems like Curt Scott has a problem with every kit car manufacturer.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That may be but, in this case Curt is being nice, they are worse than he says.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000005||pHoOl||05-24-2001||11:26 PM||||Okay, i looked at this and i didn't see anywhere that it was American dollars.  since the company is based in canada, i'm assuming canadian.  and the price works out to just under 3000 american just to let you all know.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Songman||05-25-2001||12:12 AM||||Well, I wanted to see what others had heard before I said anything bad about anybody...<P>I have an old copy of 'Kit Car' and it even has his picture and stops only short of calling him the anti-christ of the kit car world.. but it was with a company prior to Ck3...<P>I also noticed on the site that the pictured seemed to be of cars sitting on a Ferrari sales lot... <P>Just wanted to get some opinions. They do look like beautiful cars though...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||VISCERAL||05-25-2001||08:56 AM||||Blaine said he'll sell the side mirrors for $250. The look alot better than stock. They will mount on the triangle on the window frame not the door.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Archie||05-25-2001||10:14 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by VISCERAL:<BR><B>Blaine said he'll sell the side mirrors for $250. The look alot better than stock. They will mount on the triangle on the window frame not the door.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I guess I'll help you keep from making a major mistake. <P>When the mirrors are mounted on the triangle area, you can't open the door all the way with the window up without hitting the mirror.<P>On my F-40, when I wanted the mirror mounted in that area, I made a bracket to mount the mirror to the inside edge of the door panel. When the door was closed it LOOKED like the mirror was mounted to the Triangle area but when you opened the door the mirror opened with the door. I can find some pics. of this if you need them.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000009||Rob Durham||05-25-2001||10:31 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B> That may be but, in this case Curt is being nice, they are worse than he says.<P>Archie</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Archie is very correct in his statement, I have had some dealings with CK3, they put out nice litature but thats as far as it gets unless you like to throw away your money.<P>The address in Las Vegas was for a Mail Box Ect. same with the addy they had in CA and WA.<P>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000010||cowans||05-25-2001||11:20 AM||||Boy, have I been waiting for a post like this. I purchased a F40 from CK3 last Feb 2000. I can tell you that their fiberglass is excellent...That the good side!!! They have more excuses than "Carter has pills!!!". I have charged back through Mastercard twice (sucessfully) for undeliverables! If you choose do purchase anything from this company, DO NOT PAY UPFRONT, get a truck, be there to watch and account for everything thats loaded on it, then and only then, pay only for whats on the truck!!! I have 4 full folders of legal statements, bills, emails that will fill a hard drive, plus an enormous amount of stress with this Company. The plant is large and clean, Warren, a employee, very helpful in tech support. But, if they have you cash upfront...., you're at their mercy! Pay through a credit card, if something goes wrong, you can charge-back for it.... funny thing is, it was Blaine who taught me this!!!<BR>Sandy<BR>Ps email me for 2gig full story!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||cowans||05-25-2001||03:09 PM||||Archie is right on about the mirrors. you need to fabricate a steel triangle, bolt/weld to the door window slot, that will act as a mount for the mirrors. And the mirror is just a fiberglass shell, you need to dismantle your fiero electric mirror, mount the motor in the shell, remove the plastic backing mount to the actual mirror glass and fabricate the oval shape of the inside shell, and finally attach the oval mirror to the plastic backing. Spend your money on some late model Corvette mirrors, they will mount to the doors. Sandy<BR>P,S. CK3 works in U.S. dollars!||||reg||9
Z||000012||Voytek||05-25-2001||05:55 PM||||U.S. bucks is absolutely right.<BR>The local rumor is that CK3 is in some trouble over copyright with Ferrari.  Apparently they won't be making Ferrari kits much longer.  Maybe the prices are some kind of 'lawsuit specials'.  I don't know about their reputation.  I've tried to see what they do and went to the plant.  They woudn't show me anything and their yard is covered quite well.  In fact they were pretty tight lipped about ANYTHING they do.  The credit card and not paying up front advice is good advice.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Voytek||05-25-2001||06:04 PM||||Oh, the kit does look VERY SWEET (wiping off drool).||||reg||1
Z||000014||gabriel||05-26-2001||02:57 PM||||&gt;The local rumor is that CK3 is in some trouble over copyright with Ferrari. Apparently they won't be making Ferrari kits much longer. Maybe the prices are some kind of 'lawsuit spec<P>  Maybe someone should inquire as to how much they want for the molds.<P>  I can obtain a set for the TR, but the guy wants too much for them (they need work)<P>  Archie is correct about the mirrors.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Archie||05-26-2001||05:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by gabriel:<BR><B>  Maybe someone should inquire as to how much they want for the molds.<P>  I can obtain a set for the TR, but the guy wants too much for them (they need work)<P>  Archie is correct about the mirrors.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey, I'll sell you my TR molds (&/or my F-40 molds).<P>With the Fino & Finale I really don't have the time or desire to make any more of those bodies.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000016||saleenfiero||05-26-2001||07:37 PM||||INSANELY RETARDED QUESTIONS - BEWARE!<P>How are these molds used to form the bodies?<BR>What are the friggin' things worth?||||reg||1
Z||000017||Songman||05-26-2001||08:04 PM||||You form the fiberglass panels on the inside of the molds....<P>I almost bought a set of.. I think it was 328 molds. Was bidding on eBay and was willing to go about $2500. Archie bid on them also and both of us quit before we got up that high... <P>So I would say it depends on the car, and how many kits you think you can sell.. Also depends on if you know how to form fiberglass or will have to pay someone to do it for you. <P>Archie.. comments?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000018||TRiAD||05-26-2001||08:31 PM||||Hi. I'm new, this is my first post. I don't even own a Fiero yet, and am just now planning my project out. <BR>I love the TR body styles, and thought these guys might be a good way to accomplish that. <P>I got the same email you did. I came here to complete my registration, and change my password, and saw this post on top. <P>I have met Archie, and I trust him. If he recommends someone (like he did EuroWorks to me) I trust it. Likewise, if he says Curt was being kind, I have a tendancy to believe it. <P>I emailed Blaine. Here it is...<BR>------------------------<BR>Blaine.<BR>I'm not one to believe everything I hear or read, but there seems to be some concern in the Fiero and kit communities regarding the service of your company.  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/007652.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/007652.html</A> <BR>I am still interested, but wanted you to know there are concerns and I am aware of them. <BR>I tend to be too trusting at times, but recently [had a bad experience].<BR>I you are planning on continuing in business, and to support these models you currently offer, then we can still most likely do some business. But I must give you fair warning...I reward excellent service, and I [tell everyone about bad service]. <P>If you are still interested, I look forward to helping you rebuild your reputation. <BR>------------------------<P>Anyways, thought I'd put in my $.02.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><B><I>Looking for a white '88 GT 5 sp</I></B>||||reg||4
Z||000019||Songman||05-27-2001||12:17 AM||||Well, I guess I won't be getting any more e-mails from Ck3.. or worse, maybe hate mail or e-mail bombs... heheh<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000020||TRiAD||05-28-2001||09:20 PM||||Songman, sorry, I hope you don't think I burned you withg them there. Fact is, if they are this way, it's better we avoid them anyway, and if seeing this would make them better, then we all benefit, right?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Anyways, here's his response. <P>-----------------------------------<BR>Michael<P>Thanks for the heads up. We stopped reading lists like this many many years<BR>ago. TALK IS CHEAP, as Curt Scott if he every took up our paid visit to our<BR>30,000 square foot plant. Ask V8 Archie about his facility. If we depended on<BR>the Kit buying public to buy kits, we would unfortunatly not have a 30,000<BR>square<BR>foot facility and deliver the number of vehciles that we do. Ask SAndy Cowan<BR>if he just scammed us out of $10,000 or so. I can tell you this, there is no<BR>one in the kit car industry who has, on any level the ability to design,<BR>manufacter<BR>and deliver the quality of vehicles that we do. So that brings us to ur point,<BR>the only reason we emailed the promo out was that we get 200 - 250 request a<BR>week for kits, if you look at our webiste you will see no mention of kit sales.<BR>Your comment on if we are planning to continue on in business, we might be able<BR>to do some business, well we haven't gone any where in the past nor are we.<BR>Nevertheless, all of the diatribe aside TALK IS CHEAP. If you want to talk<BR>further<BR>feel free to email me or call me on Monday at 800 454 7627 ext 250 we are<BR>working<BR>monday as it is a holiday<P>Best Regards<P>Blaine Kennedy<BR>-------------------------------<P>I won't be returning his email. Anyone who would openly air their laundry, or insult someone I said I trust, isn't gettign my business. Ever. <BR>"Ask Archie about his facility..." he says. I've been there, and no, it's no 30,000 sq ft facility, but who needs one for what Archie does? A 30,000 sq ft facility would be overkill and fiscally irresponsible for Archie's current offerings. I was very impressed by Archie's honesty, willing to spend time with a couple of bozos (my brother and I) when we drove up there, and his interest in my project. <P>Anyway, thought I'd keep you posted.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR><B><I>Looking for a white '88 GT 5 sp</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000021||SPDFREK||05-28-2001||09:49 PM||||one thing to remember, everything starts small! And besides all that, look at Vector, sweet cars-all hand made (me thinks)-and from what I understand made in a small facility. anyway, I would rather buy from a small place that pays attention to detail, then a big place that pumps them out with imperfections!<BR>my two cents.||||reg||4
Z||000022||cowans||05-28-2001||10:56 PM||||Well. I won't yet air my dirty laundry. But, Blaine, scamming you for $10 grand. That's quite a statement!!! It's funny though, the more research I did on CK3, the more the stories were the same!!!! Oh God, I feel another headache coming on!!!!!!<BR>Sandy||||reg||8
