Z||000027||TRiAD||05-29-2001||09:34 PM||||Thanks guys, I appreciate the support. <BR>Blaine sent me another nasy-gram, too Archie. Here goes...<BR>--------------------------------<BR>Michael<BR> <BR>I thought I would get back to you, as you said you would not be getting back to me on the Pennock's Fiero mailing list. As for Archie, it was Archie was who said we were misleading a client on a mirror purchase, you can read the list. As for our openly airing our dirty laundry, don't you actually mean honestly replying to your questions posed in a email of 05/26/01! Nevertheless, these kind of shenanigans are the fundamental basis for why we don't advertise or pursue the retail kit business, talk is cheap and the proof is obviously in the final products of which we will out our up against any individual or company in the market today!. Should you have any questions that you would like answered or we can help you we would be glad to do what we can. <BR> <BR>Best Regards<BR> <BR>Blaine Kennedy<BR>800 454 7627 ext 250 <BR> <BR> <BR>PS    I emailed Archie commenting on his slamming our offering to sell a set of mirrors to a guy, I find it humorous that you would email me and ask me about a V8 kit and body kit, while Archie is openly slamming us! Hmmm Feel free to post the message in it's entirety to the Pennock's Fiero mailing list<BR>----------------------------------<BR><I>"I find it humorous that you would email me and ask me about a V8 kit and body kit, while Archie is openly slamming us!"</I><P>Um, I didn't even know they offered V8 kits...only rebodies. You know, the more he talks, the less he makes sense...or the less I listen...either way. It's a shame, really. Nice looking kits, beautiful website, and a loose nut behind the wheel.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Sorry for the crap they're saying about you, Archie. At least no one here doesn't know he's a blow-hard. <BR>Blaine, if you send me nasty email from this, I will block your address. If you respond, keep it clean. <P>------------------<BR><B><I>Looking for a white '88 GT 5 sp</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000028||cowans||05-29-2001||10:08 PM||||Well, I've been this thread with alot of interest. To those that are interested in purchasing a KIT... Make sure the  Company can supply you with names/contacts of previous customers for references! Sandy||||reg||10
Z||000029||SPDFREK||05-30-2001||05:15 PM||||OK, CK3 must be watching this thread cause I have 2 Emails from CK3 bout their kit. and I have to say If I were not as broke as I am I would prolly try them out just to see if I could get the car looking like that. regardless it is a nice looking Pic of the car, My question is though- is the car in the Pic an actual kit, or the actual car the kit was made off of? 2) did a professional put it together, or did some employee randomly picked? CK3 if indeed you are watching the posts here, why not give us a little insight on this I know I would like to see what the answers would be.<BR>THX SPDFREK<p>[This message has been edited by SPDFREK (edited 05-30-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000030||cowans||06-26-2001||09:10 AM||||Well, I just received a phone call and some emails from a lawyer in Calgary. Apparently, CK3 has taken an American friend for big $$$. He,(so I'm told) sent CK3 50%(cheque)of the total for a 355 replica a couple of months ago, and apparently, nothing has been done. I have not confirmed this with Blaine Kennedy.<BR> It's too bad as their product is very good...just receiving it.... Pay with a Credit Card...Credit Card Companies have alot of clout! Should you not receive what you purchased, they will chase down the seller for you, or, credit your card!<BR>Sandy||||reg||1
